# SS-25 - First public release v1.0.0
Workstream ID: SS-25
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/StonksSniper/issues/25
Status: DONE
Milestone: M4
Dependencies: SS-20, SS-21, SS-22, SS-23, SS-24

## Purpose
Publish the current educational application as its first non-prerelease,
with a complete Windows download, corresponding source and clear limitations.
Keep earlier prerelease tags and assets immutable.

## Tasks
- [x] Set v1.0.0, refresh release-facing README/guides and packaging metadata.
- [x] Make hosted Windows artifact paths follow the application version.
- [x] Run local checks and exact-source hosted tests, live checks and frozen runtime.
- [x] Verify asset receipts/checksums and publish v1.0.0 as the latest stable release.
- [x] Download published assets again and verify exact identity/source/tag.
- [x] Celebrate the verified milestone and persist release continuity.

## Acceptance criteria
- README download and setup instructions point to the first public release.
- Windows EXE includes the current companion, learning demos and Market tools desk.
- Public Python wheel/source support the headless lab; GUI-only EXE is not called a CLI.
- Exact tagged source matches the qualified build receipt and hosted run.
- Downloaded assets match the checksums; corresponding source/notices remain available.
- Unsigned status, provider dependence, simulation scope and unfinished roadmap stay clear.
- Existing user windows/environments, security controls and earlier releases stay unchanged.

## Completion evidence
- Local candidate: 357 passed, 4 skipped, normal exit; Ruff lint/format, strict
  mypy and whitespace passed. After fixing the stale README download artwork,
  54 affected learning/tracking cases passed and 60 local guide links resolved.
- Published https://github.com/Zanark/StonksSniper/releases/tag/v1.0.0 as latest,
  non-draft/non-prerelease at 883c941a4b721b190368da60906677ca745c48e5.
- Exact-source live CI 45155983942 passed Windows/Python 3.13.14 and Linux/Python
  3.11, actual provider checks and the real frozen Windows runtime. The EXE
  fetched 494 HDFCBANK observations and exercised 27 normal/27 date-range routes.
- Six public assets downloaded again, all byte-identical to qualified originals.
  Five payload checksums, 33 build-input hashes (exact checkout newline variants),
  330 notices entries, clean source receipt and public PE version verified.
- Python wheel/source distribution built; extracted wheel imported outside the
  checkout and returned all 27 headless strategies. Anonymous EXE/source URLs
  returned HTTP 200. No signing/local policy bypass or earlier release replacement.
- User-requested MeshBoard celebration published and read back with a fitting
  original GIF; owned release continuity updated. No external social account
  publication, fabricated peer response or roadmap completion is implied.
- Earlier source d0981dc passed 357 local tests and exact-source Windows/Linux CI;
  that evidence alone does not qualify the new versioned release.

## Completion log
- 2026-11-23: User explicitly designates this as the first public release and
  authorizes release publication, README update and a social celebration.
  Selected v1.0.0 as the first stable educational milestone, not full roadmap completion.
- 2026-11-23: Published and verified the qualified release and all downloaded
  assets; updated README/guides, celebrated on MeshBoard and retained evidence.
